USER PROMPT
Score this proposal against historical analogues.

TITLE:        The Unveiling
LOGLINE:      An unyielding authority figure and their compassionate caregiver uncover a vast conspiracy, forcing them to confront harsh truths and experience a profound loss of innocence.
MOTIF TAGS:   hidden_conspiracy, loss_of_innocence
ARCHETYPES:   authority_figure, caregiver
ACT STRUCTURE: classic_three_act

COMPARISON SET
Budget band:    mid -- budget_usd >= 20000000 AND budget_usd < 80000000
Release bucket: none; do not filter on release_bucket unless the broad set has samples to spare, and say so if you do

Budget bands available, as SQL predicates on films:
    micro  budget_usd < 5000000
    low    budget_usd >= 5000000 AND budget_usd < 20000000
    mid    budget_usd >= 20000000 AND budget_usd < 80000000
    high   budget_usd >= 80000000

Query the database yourself. Start broad, narrow only while the sample count
survives, and report insufficient evidence rather than a figure standing on
fewer than 8 films.

--- FunctionCall #1: run_query ---
SELECT motif_a, motif_b,
       countMerge(sample_count) AS n_roi,
       quantileMerge(0.5)(roi_median) AS roi_median,
       countMerge(interest_sample_count) AS n_interest,
       quantileMerge(0.5)(interest_pct_median) AS interest_median
FROM mv_motif_pair_stats
WHERE (motif_a = 'hidden_conspiracy' AND motif_b = 'loss_of_innocence')
   OR (motif_a = 'loss_of_innocence' AND motif_b = 'hidden_conspiracy')
GROUP BY motif_a, motif_b
HAVING n_roi >= 8
    [GUARDRAIL ok]

